  "notes": "A punk band that became a stadium-pop songwriting machine, windowed from 1994 as the research does, which also clears Gate 2. Modelled on the punk band the sourced single sits in — 143–190 straight with the backbeat on 2&4 at speed; the 79–95 ballad/mid-tempo band is named here rather than encoded. Harmony is documented in full for the 2004 title track: **I–IV–♭VII–IV–I–♭VII** verses and **IV–I–V–I** chorus, with \"mixolydian ♭VII… the signature colour\", so both cycles are authored, `maxChords` is 6 and mixolydian outweighs plain major in the scales. Three drum deltas are quoted: \"straight 8th kick with the snare on 2&4 at high tempo\" (a 4–8 density on all four anchors), \"a marching 16th snare figure as the intro/interlude device\" (the snare roll pinned to 16ths with almost no gap and an even grouping), and \"crash on every second bar\" with \"one-bar 16th tom runs\" as the fills, which is the crash/tom perc block. The bass is \"roots with a pick, 8ths at tempo, occasionally taking the melody line when guitars drop out\": `mirror_kick` at 0.92, a shade looser than a pure lock because of that last clause. ⚠ The **INFERRED** parameters are every drum probability and `bpm.mode` 165 — the research gives a tempo band, not a centre.",
